  "notes": "{愛|め}でる is a literary and refined verb for appreciating beauty, especially in nature.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pattern: ～を{愛|め}でる\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{愛|め}でている describes the ongoing act of appreciating beauty.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {花|はな}を{愛|め}でる: to admire flowers\n- {月|つき}を{愛|め}でる: to admire the moon\n- {紅葉|もみじ}を{愛|め}でる: to admire autumn leaves\n- {桜|さくら}を{愛|め}でる: to admire cherry blossoms\n\nRELATED WORDS:\nThe word {愛|め}でたい (auspicious, happy) is derived from the same root. The noun form {愛|め}で (appreciation, admiration) exists but is rare in modern usage.\n\nREGISTER:\nSlightly literary and elevated. In everyday speech, {鑑賞|かんしょう}する (to appreciate) or {楽|たの}しむ (to enjoy) are more common, but {愛|め}でる carries a distinctly Japanese aesthetic sensibility.",
